.TH COF-GEN 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof-gen \- Generate an orchestration from a natural language prompt,
single-shot. Drives \fBagents/meta_orchestrator.yml\fR. For a multi-turn,
clarifying-questions build instead, see \fBcof wizard\fR
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof gen [OPTIONS] {name} {prompt}
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates a new orchestration from a natural-language prompt, single-shot, by
driving the bundled agents/meta_orchestrator.yml orchestration. For a
multi-turn, clarifying-questions build instead, see cof wizard.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B NAME
Name for the generated orchestration (used as filename).
.TP
.B PROMPT
Natural language description of the orchestration to generate.
.TP
.B --out, -o
\fIOUT\fR Write the generated orchestration here (default: ./<name>.<ext>).
.TP
.B --live-state
\fILIVE_STATE\fR Mirror the generation run's state JSON to this file while it
goes. For live monitoring \(em not the generated orchestration.
.TP
.B --config, -c
\fICONFIG\fR Path to config JSON.
.TP
.B --verbose, -v
Show detailed progress.
.TP
.B --format, -f
\fIOUTPUT_FORMAT\fR Output format: yaml, json, or toon. [default: yaml]
.TP
.B --retries, -r
\fIRETRIES\fR Max retry attempts per prompt on failure. [default: 3]
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cof gen my-flow 'summarize a URL and post it to slack'
Generates my-flow.yml from a prompt.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_CONFIG
An explicit config JSON path (same as --config). When set, replaces the global
config and any project config entirely, rather than layering on top of them.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_MODEL
Overrides the resolved config's default_model.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER
Overrides the resolved config's default_adapter.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER_URL
Overrides the resolved default adapter's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_COMFYUI_URL
Overrides the comfyui plugin's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_SYSTEMONE_URL
Overrides the systemone plugin's base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_ADAPTERS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_adapters.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_PLUGINS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_plugins.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_TOOLS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_tools.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENVIRONMENT
Overrides the resolved config's environment (dev, prod, or test).
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_TRUST_PROJECT_CONFIG
Trusts a project config in the current directory without running cof trust
first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/config.json
The global config, applied first; a trusted project config layers on top of
it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/.env
Private environment variables, loaded before config resolution (written by cof
setup).
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/trusted.json
Project configs trusted by cof trust; config resolution consults it before
applying a discovered project config.
.TP
.I ./circuitry.config.json, ./config.json
A project config in the working directory, layered on top of the global config
once trusted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or the input was invalid.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option or missing argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcof(1)\fR, \fBcof-wizard(1)\fR, \fBcof-run(1)\fR
